<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Evolution of Pseudo-label Predictions</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix A Evolution of Pseudo-label Predictions ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the evolution of pseudo-label predictions of our method under the arbitrary unlabeled data distribution, evaluated on CIFAR-10-LT. From Fig. <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix A Evolution of Pseudo-label Predictions ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we observe that our CPG progressively increases the utilization rate of pseudo-labels while maintaining the high accuracy. The predicted distribution gradually approximates the ground-truth unlabeled data distribution, and the Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence between the predicted and ground-truth unlabeled data distributions decreases during training.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F5.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03993v1/LP1.svg" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/108;" width="153" height="108"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F5.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03993v1/LP2.svg" id="A1.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/108;" width="153" height="108"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F5.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03993v1/LP3.svg" id="A1.F5.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/108;" width="153" height="108"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F5.fig4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03993v1/LP4.svg" id="A1.F5.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/108;" width="153" height="108"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F5.fig5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03993v1/LP5.svg" id="A1.F5.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/108;" width="153" height="108"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F5.fig6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03993v1/LP6.svg" id="A1.F5.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/108;" width="153" height="108"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Evolution of pseudo-label predictions of our method under arbitrary unlabeled data distribution. GT denotes the ground-truth unlabeled data distribution. TP (FP) denotes the predicted true (false) positive pseudo-labels. KL denotes the Kullback-Leibler divergence between the predicted and ground-truth unlabeled data distributions. The dataset is CIFAR-10-LT with <math id="A1.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{max},M_{max},\gamma_{l},\gamma_{u})=(400,4600,50,50)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4600</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{max},M_{max},\gamma_{l},\gamma_{u})=(400,4600,50,50)</annotation></semantics></math>. Our CPG can progressively increase the utilization rate of pseudo-labels while maintaining the high accuracy during training, as the pseudo-label distribution gradually approximates the ground-truth unlabeled data distribution.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Generalization Error). ‣ 3.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first copy the Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Generalization Error). ‣ 3.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> here.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Generalization Error). ‣ 3.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span> <span id="A2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the loss function <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{la}(f(x),y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{la}(f(x),y)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{1,\dots,C\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{1,\dots,C\}</annotation></semantics></math> and upper-bounded by <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the pseudo-labeling error rate <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\epsilon&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\epsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\upsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\upsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq R_{0}-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\lambda_{t}+U\sum_{t=1}^{T}\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq R_{0}-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\lambda_{t}+U\sum_{t=1}^{T}\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the total number of training steps, <math id="A2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the model empirical risk at the final training step and initial training step (without pseudo-labels), respectively, and <math id="A2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the pseudo-labeling error rate at the <math id="A2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th training step.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first restate the definition of the model empirical risk <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> at the <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th training step, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t}=R_{t-1}-\lambda_{t}+I_{\epsilon_{t}}+I_{O_{t}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t}=R_{t-1}-\lambda_{t}+I_{\epsilon_{t}}+I_{O_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the model empirical risk at the <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th training step, <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the empirical risk reduction achieved, and <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\epsilon_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\epsilon_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{O_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{O_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the impact of noisy pseudo-labels and number of training samples, respectively. We derive <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\epsilon_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\epsilon_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{O_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{O_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> below, omitting the subscript <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> for brevity.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define the true risk on the training dataset with respect to the classification model <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R(f)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)}\left[\ell_{la}(f(x),y)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R(f)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)}\left[\ell_{la}(f(x),y)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We aim to learn a good classification model by minimizing the empirical risk <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}(f)=\widehat{R}_{l}(f)+\widehat{R}_{u}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}(f)=\widehat{R}_{l}(f)+\widehat{R}_{u}(f)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{l}(f)=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\ell_{la}(f(x_{i}),y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{l}(f)=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\ell_{la}(f(x_{i}),y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{u}(f)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{j=1}^{M}\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),y_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{u}(f)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{j=1}^{M}\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),y_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> representing the empirical risk on labeled and unlabeled training dataset, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we derive the uniform deviation bound <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{O}</annotation></semantics></math> between the true risk <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(f)</annotation></semantics></math> and the empirical risk <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> using the following lemma.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the loss function <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{la}(f(x),y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{la}(f(x),y)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{1,\dots,C\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{1,\dots,C\}</annotation></semantics></math> and upper-bounded by <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\upsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\upsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)|\leq 2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2(N+M)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)|\leq 2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2(N+M)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the function space <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> for the label <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{1,\dots,C\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{1,\dots,C\}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{h:x\longmapsto f_{y}(x)|f\in\mathcal{F}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{h:x\longmapsto f_{y}(x)|f\in\mathcal{F}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">In order to prove this lemma, we define the Rademacher complexity of the composition of loss function <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{la}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{la}</annotation></semantics></math> and model <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> labeled and <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> unlabeled training samples as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\ell_{la}\circ\mathcal{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\ell_{la}\circ\mathcal{F})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(x,y,\mu)}\left[\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\Big(\ell_{la}\big(f(x_{i}),y_{i}\big)\Big)+\sum_{j=1}^{M}\mu_{j}\Big(\ell_{la}\big(f(x_{j}),y_{j}\big)\Big)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(x,y,\mu)}\left[\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\Big(\ell_{la}\big(f(x_{i}),y_{i}\big)\Big)+\sum_{j=1}^{M}\mu_{j}\Big(\ell_{la}\big(f(x_{j}),y_{j}\big)\Big)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\mathcal{H}_{y})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\mathcal{H}_{y}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\circ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∘</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\circ</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the function composition operator, <math id="A2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{(x,y,\mu)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{(x,y,\mu)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the expectation over <math id="A2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Rademacher variable, <math id="A2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the supremum (or least upper bound) over the function set <math id="A2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> of model <math id="A2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>. The second line holds because of the Rademacher vector contraction inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we proceed with the proof by showing that the one direction <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded with probability at least <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\upsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\upsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>, and the other direction <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\widehat{R}(f)-R(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\widehat{R}(f)-R(f)</annotation></semantics></math> can be proved similarly. Note that replacing a sample <math id="A2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> leads to a change of <math id="A2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> at most <math id="A2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{U}{N+M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{U}{N+M}</annotation></semantics></math> due to the fact that <math id="A2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{la}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{la}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. According to the McDiarmid’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, for any <math id="A2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\upsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\upsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)\right]+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2(N+M)}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)\right]+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2(N+M)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to the result in  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> that shows <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)\right]\leq 2\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\mathcal{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)\right]\leq 2\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\mathcal{F})</annotation></semantics></math>, and further considering the other direction <math id="A2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\widehat{R}(f)-R(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\widehat{R}(f)-R(f)</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\upsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\upsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}|R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)|\leq 2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2(N+M)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}|R(f)-\widehat{R}(f)|\leq 2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{N+M}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2(N+M)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">In SSL, we cannot minimize the empirical risk <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{u}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{u}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> directly, since the ground-truth labels are inaccessible for unlabeled training data. Therefore, we need to train the model with <math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)=\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)=\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the pseudo-label of unlabeled sample <math id="A2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{M}</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the pseudo-labels identified by the dynamic controllable filtering. Let <math id="A2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}=\operatorname{argmin}_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\widehat{R}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>argmin</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}=\operatorname{argmin}_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\widehat{R}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> be the empirical risk minimizer, and <math id="A2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}=\operatorname{argmin}_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmin</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}=\operatorname{argmin}_{f\in\mathcal{F}}R(f)</annotation></semantics></math> be the true risk minimizer. Let <math id="A2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{ours}=\frac{1}{N+\hat{M}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\ell_{la}(f(x_{i}),y_{i})+\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{ours}=\frac{1}{N+\hat{M}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\ell_{la}(f(x_{i}),y_{i})+\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})\right]</annotation></semantics></math> be the training loss on <math id="A2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> labeled and <math id="A2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{M}</annotation></semantics></math> pseudo-labeled samples with pseudo-labeling error rate <math id="A2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for our method.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we can bound the difference <math id="A2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\epsilon_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\epsilon_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="A2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{u}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{u}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> as follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the loss function <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{la}(f(x),y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{la}(f(x),y)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{1,\dots,C\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{1,\dots,C\}</annotation></semantics></math> and upper-bounded by <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the pseudo-labeling error rate <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\epsilon&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\epsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq|\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)-\widehat{R}_{u}(f)|\leq U\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq|\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)-\widehat{R}_{u}(f)|\leq U\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let’s first expand <math id="A2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\left[(1-\epsilon)\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),y_{j})+\frac{\epsilon}{C-1}\sum_{c=1}^{C}\mathbb{I}(\hat{y}_{j}\neq y_{j})\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\left[(1-\epsilon)\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),y_{j})+\frac{\epsilon}{C-1}\sum_{c=1}^{C}\mathbb{I}(\hat{y}_{j}\neq y_{j})\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we show its upper bound:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{R}_{u}^{\prime}(f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{u}(f)+\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\left[\frac{\epsilon}{C-1}\sum_{c=1}^{C}\mathbb{I}(\hat{y}_{j}\neq y_{j})\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{u}(f)+\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\left[\frac{\epsilon}{C-1}\sum_{c=1}^{C}\mathbb{I}(\hat{y}_{j}\neq y_{j})\ell_{la}(f(x_{j}),\hat{y}_{j})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{u}(f)+\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\left[\frac{\epsilon}{C-1}\sum_{c=1}^{C}\mathbb{I}(\hat{y}_{j}\neq y_{j})U\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{u}(f)+\frac{1}{\hat{M}}\sum_{j=1}^{\hat{M}}\left[\frac{\epsilon}{C-1}\sum_{c=1}^{C}\mathbb{I}(\hat{y}_{j}\neq y_{j})U\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{u}(f)+U\epsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{u}(f)+U\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">and when <math id="A2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, it reaches the lower bound <math id="A2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{u}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{u}(f)</annotation></semantics></math>, which concludes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Based on the above lemmas, for any <math id="A2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\upsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\upsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, at the <math id="A2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th training step, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t}(\hat{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t}(\hat{f})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t}(\hat{f})+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t}(\hat{f})+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t_{l}}(\hat{f})+\widehat{R}_{t_{u}}(\hat{f})+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t_{l}}(\hat{f})+\widehat{R}_{t_{u}}(\hat{f})+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t_{l}}(\hat{f})+\widehat{R}_{t_{u}}^{\prime}(\hat{f})+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t_{l}}(\hat{f})+\widehat{R}_{t_{u}}^{\prime}(\hat{f})+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t_{l}}(f)+\widehat{R}_{t_{u}}^{\prime}(f)+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t_{l}}(f)+\widehat{R}_{t_{u}}^{\prime}(f)+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t_{l}}(f)+\widehat{R}_{t_{u}}(f)+U\epsilon_{t}+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t_{l}}(f)+\widehat{R}_{t_{u}}(f)+U\epsilon_{t}+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t}(f)+U\epsilon_{t}+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\widehat{R}_{t}(f)+U\epsilon_{t}+2\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq R_{t}(f)+U\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq R_{t}(f)+U\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first and seventh lines are based on Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and three and fifth lines are due to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The fourth line is by the definition of <math id="A2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we can derive <math id="A2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\epsilon_{t}}+I_{O_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\epsilon_{t}}+I_{O_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{\epsilon_{t}}+I_{O_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{\epsilon_{t}}+I_{O_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|\widehat{R}_{t}^{\prime}(f)-\widehat{R}_{t}(f)|+|R_{t}(f)-\widehat{R}_{t}(f)|=|\widehat{R}_{t}^{\prime}(f)-R_{t}(f)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|\widehat{R}_{t}^{\prime}(f)-\widehat{R}_{t}(f)|+|R_{t}(f)-\widehat{R}_{t}(f)|=|\widehat{R}_{t}^{\prime}(f)-R_{t}(f)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq U\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq U\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting Eq. (<a href="#A2.E22" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) into Eq. (<a href="#A2.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) yields:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{\begin{aligned} R_{t}&amp;\leq R_{t-1}-\lambda_{t}+U\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}},\\
R_{t-1}&amp;\leq R_{t-2}-\lambda_{t-1}+U\epsilon_{t-1}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t-1}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t-1}}},\\
&amp;\quad\vdots\quad\\
R_{1}&amp;\leq R_{0}-\lambda_{1}+U\epsilon_{1}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{1}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{1}}}.\\
\end{aligned}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{\begin{aligned} R_{t}&amp;\leq R_{t-1}-\lambda_{t}+U\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}},\\
R_{t-1}&amp;\leq R_{t-2}-\lambda_{t-1}+U\epsilon_{t-1}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t-1}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t-1}}},\\
&amp;\quad\vdots\quad\\
R_{1}&amp;\leq R_{0}-\lambda_{1}+U\epsilon_{1}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{1}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{1}}}.\\
\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, combining the sub-equations in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) through summation yields:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq R_{0}-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\lambda_{t}+U\sum_{t=1}^{T}\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>υ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq R_{0}-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\lambda_{t}+U\sum_{t=1}^{T}\epsilon_{t}+4\sqrt{2}\rho\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{y=1}^{C}\mathcal{R}_{O_{t}}(\mathcal{H}_{y})+2U\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{2}{\upsilon}}{2O_{t}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">At this point, we have proven Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Generalization Error). ‣ 3.4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Proposed Method ‣ Keep It on a Leash: Controllable Pseudo-label Generation Towards Realistic Long-Tailed Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Dataset Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform our experiments on four widely-used datasets (CIFAR-10-LT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, CIFAR-100-LT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, Food-101-LT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, and SVHN-LT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>), following the main experimental settings in FreeMatch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> and SimPro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, details are as below.</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CIFAR-10-LT</em>: We test nine settings with <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{max},M_{max})=(400,4600)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4600</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{max},M_{max})=(400,4600)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\{100,150,200\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>100,150,200</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\{100,150,200\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The unlabeled data follows either the same long-tailed distribution as the labeled data (consistent case), or an inverse long-tailed or arbitrary distribution (inconsistent cases).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CIFAR-100-LT</em>: We examine nine settings with <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{max},M_{max})=(50,450)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>50,450</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{max},M_{max})=(50,450)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\{10,15,20\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\{10,15,20\}</annotation></semantics></math>, using the same consistent/inconsistent unlabeled data distribution patterns as above.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Food-101-LT</em>: We evaluate six settings with <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{max},M_{max})=(50,450)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>50,450</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{max},M_{max})=(50,450)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\{10,15\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\{10,15\}</annotation></semantics></math>, maintaining the same distribution cases.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SVHN-LT</em>: We evaluate three settings with <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{max},M_{max},\gamma)=(50,450,100)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>50,450,100</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{max},M_{max},\gamma)=(50,450,100)</annotation></semantics></math>, following the same distribution scheme.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the default settings and hyperparameters in USB, i.e., the batch size of labeled data <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to 64, while unlabeled data <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to 7 times <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the confidence threshold <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is set to 0.95. Moreover, we use the WRN-28-2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> architecture, the SGD optimizer with momentum 0.9, and weight decay 5e-4 for training. We use a cosine learning rate decay <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite> scheme, which sets the learning rate to <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\cos\left(\frac{7\pi t}{16T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\cos\left(\frac{7\pi t}{16T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where the initial learning rate <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is set to 0.03, <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the current training step, and the total number of training steps <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>18</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{18}</annotation></semantics></math>. We repeat each experiment with three different random seeds (i.e., 0, 1, and 2) and report the mean and standard deviation of the performances. We conduct the experiments on a single NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPU using PyTorch v2.3.1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>More Experiment Results and Analyses</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Comparison of Macro-F1 on CIFAR-10-LT and CIFAR-100-LT</h3>

<figure id="A5.T7" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:64%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Comparison of Macro-F1 (<math id="A5.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>%</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%</annotation></semantics></math>) on CIFAR-10-LT (<math id="A5.T7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{max}=400,M_{max}=4600,\gamma=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4600</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{max}=400,M_{max}=4600,\gamma=100</annotation></semantics></math>) and CIFAR-100-LT (<math id="A5.T7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{max}=50,M_{max}=450,\gamma=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>450</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{max}=50,M_{max}=450,\gamma=10</annotation></semantics></math>) under different unlabeled data distributions.</figcaption>
