</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Broader Impacts</h2>

<div id="A10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper presents work whose goal is to advance the field of Machine Learning. Specifically, we propose a new realistic long-tailed semi-supervised learning algorithm to improve performance in unknown arbitrary distribution scenarios by expanding the labeled dataset with the progressively identified reliable pseudo-labels from the unlabeled dataset and training the model on the updated labeled dataset with a known distribution, making it unaffected by the unlabeled data distribution. We further theoretically prove that this iterative process can significantly reduce the generalization error under some conditions. There are many potential societal consequences of our work, none which we feel must be specifically highlighted here.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
